# Requests for manual testing (VS Code REST Client, Rider, Visual Studio).
# Run them top to bottom: later requests use IDs from earlier responses.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5080

### Genres
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/genres

### Create a movie
# @name createMovie
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/movies
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Alien",
  "releaseDate": "1979-05-25",
  "runtimeMinutes": 117,
  "tmdbId": 348,
  "genreIds": [27, 878]
}

### Get the movie
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/movies/{{createMovie.response.body.$.id}}

### Search movies
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/movies?search=ali&sort=-releaseDate&page=1&pageSize=10

### Validation error: missing title (model validation runs before the genre check)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/movies
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "genreIds": [99999]
}

### Validation error: unknown property
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/movies
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Alien",
  "genreIds": [],
  "director": "Ridley Scott"
}

### Log a viewing
# @name createDiaryEntry
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/diary-entries
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "movieId": "{{createMovie.response.body.$.id}}",
  "watchedOn": "2026-10-31",
  "rating": 9,
  "review": "Still terrifying.",
  "liked": true
}

### Diary
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/diary-entries?from=2026-01-01

### Delete the movie (expected: 409, it has a diary entry)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/movies/{{createMovie.response.body.$.id}}

### Put the movie on the watchlist
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/watchlist/{{createMovie.response.body.$.id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "note": "Rewatch the director's cut"
}

### Watchlist
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/watchlist
